      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T14:55:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How do we change the config for 1 alarm only?  If the device has 1000 alarms in its config and I want to change only 1 of them, how do i do that?",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_c748e8ce",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000127
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T17:42:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming the device ID is 123456789, and you would like to SUPPRESS just one Alarm \"Alarm1000\"out of 1000 alarms configured, use this RPC and body should be as below.\n\n{\n  \"id\": \"123456789\",\n  \"alarm_cfg\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"SUPPRESS\",\n      \"name\": \"Alarm1000\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nWhen the simulated adapter gets the update alarm config request, it would take care to just SUPPRESS this alarm of 1000 configured alarms. The 999 other alarms would remain unaffected.\nI have verified such a test case to be working fine.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_c7c34837",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_275fa474",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
